# Caddy in front of the Poise gateway (docs/Operating.md). Caddy holds the
# certificates: the apex's, obtained at start, and one for each workspace
# host, obtained on its first visit once the gateway confirms the host belongs
# to someone (on-demand TLS).
#
# Every request reaches the gateway with the browser's Host. Caddy passes
# WebSockets through and puts no time limit on a proxied response or
# WebSocket, so event streams, the Chat WebSocket and terminals stay open as
# long as both ends keep them open.
#
# With no trusted_proxies, Caddy replaces any X-Forwarded-For,
# X-Forwarded-Proto and X-Forwarded-Host a client sends with what it saw
# itself. The gateway extends Caddy's X-Forwarded-For, sets the other two
# itself, and drops Forwarded, any other X-Forwarded-* header and
# X-Poise-Identity, so no client can pose as another address, scheme, host
# or person.
{
	email {$POISE_ACME_EMAIL}
	on_demand_tls {
		# Caddy asks with Host: gateway:8080, the only Host the gateway answers this for.
		ask http://gateway:8080/_gateway/tls-ask
	}
}

{$POISE_DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy gateway:8080
}

*.{$POISE_DOMAIN} {
	tls {
		on_demand
	}
	reverse_proxy gateway:8080
}
